{"id":"lem:all-beta-oracle-lower-floor","kind":"lemma","statement":"For every admissible \(\alpha,\beta,s,d,M_Y,L,pbar,c,t_0\), there is a constant \(C_{\mathrm{low}}>0\), independent of \(n\), such that for every \(n\ge1\), \[\mathcal M_n(\alpha,\beta,s,d,M_Y,L,pbar,c,t_0)\ge C_{\mathrm{low}}r_n(\alpha).\] The two least-favorable laws have \(p_X(x)=1\) and \(\pi_P(a\mid x)=1\), so the lower floor is uniform over every finite treatment-density smoothness order.","free_symbols":["n","d","M_Y","L","pbar","c","t_0","alpha","beta","s","P","Pclass","P_X","p_X","Y","A","X","Z_i","mu_P","pi_P","theta_P","T_n","M_n","r_n"],"depends_on":["ass:iid","ass:mu-version","ass:pi-version","ass:px-version","ass:bounded-outcome","ass:positivity-lower","ass:positivity-upper","ass:px-bounded","ass:mu-a-holder","ass:pi-a-holder","ass:mu-x-holder","ass:pi-x-holder","prop:class-nonempty","def:holder-class","def:minimax-mse","def:oracle-rate"],"proof_tex":"Choose the explicit smooth bump \[\psi(u)=\begin{cases}\exp\!\left(1-\dfrac{1}{1-u^2}\right),&\lvert u\rvert<1,\\0,&\lvert u\rvert\ge1,\end{cases}\] so that \(\psi(0)=1\), and let \(C_{\psi,\alpha}<\infty\) bound its Hölder-\(\alpha\) norm. Put \(b=M_Y\). Choose constants \(\lambda>0\) and \(\kappa>0\), depending only on the displayed model parameters, such that \[\lambda C_{\psi,\alpha}\le L,\qquad \lambda\kappa^{\alpha}\le b/2,\qquad \kappa<\min(t_0,1-t_0),\] and impose one further smallness condition on \(\kappa\) below. For \(h_n=\kappa n^{-1/(2\alpha+1)}\) and \(\zeta\in\{-1,1\}\), define a law \(P_{\zeta}\) by taking \(X\) uniform on \([0,1]^d\), \(A\) uniform on \([0,1]\) independently of \(X\), and \(Y\in\{-b,b\}\) conditionally on \((A=a,X=x)\) with \[P_{\zeta}(Y=b\mid A=a,X=x)=\frac{1+\mu_{\zeta}(a,x)/b}{2},\qquad \mu_{\zeta}(a,x)=\zeta\lambda h_n^{\alpha}\psi\!\left(\frac{a-t_0}{h_n}\right).\] The choice of \(\lambda\) makes the scaled bump a Hölder-\(\alpha\) function of radius at most \(L\), uniformly in \(x\). At \(a=t_0\), it is constant in \(x\), so it satisfies every Hölder-\(s\) slice condition. The designated densities \(p_X=1\) and \(\pi_{P_{\zeta}}=1\) satisfy all density, positivity, and Hölder conditions, for every \(\beta>0\). The outcome is bounded by \(M_Y\), and its displayed conditional mean is \(\mu_{\zeta}\). Thus \(P_{+}\) and \(P_{-}\) belong to the frozen class. Their targets are \[\theta_{P_{\zeta}}(t_0)=\zeta\lambda h_n^{\alpha},\] so their separation is \(2\lambda h_n^{\alpha}\).

